 "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered comparisons use direction -1, so a positive signed estimate means the exposed group or level has the more negative dependency score, i.e., stronger dependency. The approximate 10% absolute-mean scales are about 0.027 for outcome_013, 0.026 for outcome_009, and 0.025 for outcome_004. None of the results meets the scientific acceptance standard: a direction-consistent 95% interval excluding zero and a point estimate at or near the clinical scale. For outcome_013, H82 feature_034 is closest in magnitude but opposite the registered direction (-0.0187, CI -0.0385 to +0.0012) and interval-crossing; H83 and H84 are small positive interval-crossing; H91 is opposite-signed and interval-crossing. For outcome_009, H85, H86, and H87 are opposite-signed and interval-crossing, while H92 is small positive and interval-crossing. For outcome_004, H89 is small positive and interval-crossing; H88, H90, and H93 are opposite-signed or essentially null with intervals crossing zero. These are unadjusted, dataset-specific contrasts with adequate cells, so the issue is not cell size. Competing explanations include unadjusted confounding, correlated predictor structure, and selection effects from repeated screening; the inconsistent signs and generally small magnitudes make a robust association unlikely. Therefore all twelve claims are rejected and closed. The only remaining interval-excluding direction-consistent signal is H103, the reversed outcome_005 feature_021 contrast with signed estimate +0.0201, CI +0.0012 to +0.0390. Its magnitude is slightly below the approximate 10% scale for outcome_005 (~0.025), but it is scientifically worth independent follow-up because the unadjusted interval excludes zero and could reflect a weaker or stronger dependency association. I am requesting validation for H103 to test whether the reversed signal replicates and whether it reaches clinical relevance. I am not validating any of H82-H93 because their intervals cross zero and none approaches the threshold in the registered direction.",
 "validate": "H103",
 "research_notes": "Accepted claims: none. H82-H93 assessed and all rejected/closed: outcome_013, outcome_009, and outcome_004 showed no direction-consistent, interval-excluding, clinically relevant association for feature_034, feature_002, feature_050, or feature_055 level_002 vs level_003. Scales used: ~0.027 outcome_013, ~0.026 outcome_009, ~0.025 outcome_004. H103 remains active unresolved; validation requested because it is the only current interval-excluding direction-consistent signal (outcome_005 feature_021, direction +1, signed +0.0201 CI +0.0012 to +0.0390), but point estimate is below approximate 10% scale ~0.025. Do not accept H103 on current discovery evidence alone. If validation is interval-excluding and clinically near/above threshold, accept; otherwise reject/close. Next analyses should proceed to H94-H102: stable nominal contrasts for outcome_002, outcome_016, outcome_007 using feature_055 l2 vs l3, feature_054 l2 vs l1, feature_063 l2 vs l1. Scales ~0.026, ~0.0256, ~0.0245. Do not validate crossed common binary screens without coherence. Validation remaining after requesting H103: 5. No causal or generalizable interpretation."
